---
description: Rules for the unverified low-level files (clone detection, treemap layout)
globs: ["Sources/DiskMapCore/CloneDetector.swift", "Sources/DiskMapCore/SquarifiedTreemap.swift"]
alwaysApply: false
---

Both files were originally written without a macOS toolchain to compile
against. `SquarifiedTreemap.swift` was verified in TASK-001 (paper
section 3.1 layout, plus a tiling test). `CloneDetector.swift` was
verified in TASK-005 against `<sys/fcntl.h>` and a real `cp -c` pair —
the header comment records the packed layout and why `F_LOG2PHYS_EXT`
is required. The checks below are the procedure, not an open warning.

For `CloneDetector.swift` specifically:
- Confirm the `log2phys` struct's field names, types, and order against the
  actual `<sys/fcntl.h>` in the active SDK
  (`xcrun --show-sdk-path`, then look under `usr/include/sys/fcntl.h`), not
  against the comment in this file.
- Confirm the `F_LOG2PHYS` constant value the same way.
- Test against a real, known clone pair before considering this done:
  `cp -c original.bin clone.bin` on an APFS volume, then confirm
  `CloneDetector.areLikelyClones` returns true for that pair and false for
  two unrelated files of the same size.
- Consider whether `F_LOG2PHYS_EXT` (multi-extent) is needed instead of the
  single-extent `F_LOG2PHYS` for files above a few KB — see the file's own
  comment for why this matters.

For `SquarifiedTreemap.swift` specifically:
- Run `swift test --filter SquarifiedTreemapTests` first. If anything
  fails, debug against the reference example in the original paper (Bruls,
  Huizing, van Wijk, "Squarified Treemaps", 2000) — sizes [6,6,4,3,2,2,1] in
  a 6x4 rectangle, Figure 6 — rather than guessing at the row-building
  logic from scratch.
- Any fix here should keep or extend the "full area, no gaps/overlaps" test
  — don't weaken that assertion to make it pass.

Once you've verified either file against a real build and real tests,
update its header comment to remove the UNVERIFIED warning and note what
you confirmed and how.
